[SIZE=5][B]OpenCredits — open-source credits for XenForo 2.3+[/B][/SIZE]

A free (MIT) credits system for XenForo 2.3+: reward activity, show balances,
let members transfer credits, gate trophies on wealth.

[B]What members get[/B]
[LIST]
[*] [B]Earn credits[/B] for posting threads/replies, receiving reactions, registering, and daily visits — amounts managed in AdminCP → Credits → Earning events.
[*] [B]Multiple currencies[/B] with a primary and per-currency visibility, all managed in AdminCP → Credits → Currencies.
[*] [B]Wallet everywhere[/B] — balances in postbit, in the account menu, and on member profiles (primary stat plus a full currencies tab). The profile wallet also carries a transfer shortcut and recent history; full per-currency history is on the Credits nav tab.
[*] [B]Transfers[/B] — send credits to another member, with username autocomplete. Transfers can never overdraw.
[*] [B]Redeem codes[/B] — coupon codes members redeem for credits (single/multi-use, expiry, one per member).
[*] [B]Earn alerts[/B] — members are notified when credits land, with per-event admin toggles, member opt-out, and a global kill switch.
[*] [B]Trophies[/B] — "has at least / fewer than X credits" criteria work with trophies, notices, and user-group promotions.
[*] [B]Leaderboard[/B] — a "Top credit holders" widget you can place on the forum home or sidebar, ranked by balance.
[*] [B]Admin tools[/B] — adjust any member's balance, rebuild balances, backfill pre-install content, prune old history into balance snapshots, display toggles, all under AdminCP → Credits.
[*] [B]Scheduling control[/B] — the daily-visit boundary follows UTC (default), board time, or a fixed UTC offset.
[*] [B]Leaderboard widget[/B] — place a "Top credit holders" widget with a configurable count and currency.
[*] [B]Built to integrate[/B] — spend/award API plus a change event other add-ons can hook. Full reference in docs/API.md on GitHub.
[/LIST]

[B]Requirements[/B]
[LIST]
[*] XenForo 2.3.0+, PHP 8.2+, MySQL 8.0+
[*] No other add-ons required.
[/LIST]

[B]Install[/B]

Grab the release zip from the [URL=https://github.com/techwiz18/open-credits/releases]releases page[/URL]. Two ways, pick one:

[B]A — from AdminCP (fastest).[/B] AdminCP → Add-ons → [B]Install from archive[/B], upload the release zip, and click [B]Install[/B]. If that option isn't available on your setup, use manual upload below.

[B]B — manual upload.[/B] Unzip the release on your computer. Inside you'll find an [ICODE]upload/[/ICODE] folder. Upload the [B]contents[/B] of [ICODE]upload/[/ICODE] into your forum root (the folder with [ICODE]index.php[/ICODE], [ICODE]src/[/ICODE], [ICODE]data/[/ICODE]) via FTP/File Manager, merging folders. Then AdminCP → Add-ons, find [B]OpenCredits[/B] and click [B]Install[/B].

Then, either way:
[LIST=1]
[*] Grant permissions: AdminCP → Groups & permissions → User groups → Registered → Credits tab → allow [B]View own credit wallet and history[/B] and [B]Transfer credits to other users[/B]. Repeat for any other groups.
[*] Members start earning on the next post/reaction/visit. Balances appear in postbit automatically.
[/LIST]

To upgrade later: upload the newer release the same way, then AdminCP → Add-ons → OpenCredits → [B]Upgrade[/B].

[B]AdminCP access[/B]

The [B]Credits[/B] AdminCP section (currencies, earning events, rebuild) is gated by the [I]Manage credits[/I] admin permission. Super admins always have access; for other admins go to Groups & permissions → Administrators → click the name → set type to Regular administrator (the permission list is hidden for super admins) → check [B]Manage credits[/B] → Save.

[B]Earning defaults[/B]
[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Action[/TH][TH]Default[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD]New thread[/TD][TD]$5.00[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Reply[/TD][TD]$1.00[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Content reacted to[/TD][TD]$2.00[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Registration[/TD][TD]$10.00[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD]Daily visit (once/day)[/TD][TD]$5.00[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]
Change amounts, add triggers, or add currencies any time in AdminCP → Credits.

[B]Troubleshooting[/B]
[LIST]
[*] [B]Balances look wrong[/B] — AdminCP → Credits → Rebuild balances (or CLI: [ICODE]php cmd.php oc-credits:rebuild[/ICODE]).
[*] [B]Permission errors[/B] — check the Credits permission tab per user group (fresh installs auto-allow them for Registered).
[*] [B]Uninstalling deletes everything[/B] — balances, ledger, events, currencies, and redeem codes.
[/LIST]

[B]Roadmap & support[/B]
[LIST]
[*] Future ideas live as [URL=https://github.com/techwiz18/open-credits/milestones]milestones[/URL] — vote and comment on [URL=https://github.com/techwiz18/open-credits/issues]issues[/URL].
[*] Source: [URL=https://github.com/techwiz18/open-credits]github.com/techwiz18/open-credits[/URL] (MIT). This project is vibe-coded with AI assistance — review security-sensitive changes before deploying.
[/LIST]

[B]Changelog[/B]

[B]0.11.0[/B]
[LIST]
[*] [B]Profile wallet[/B] — profile pages show balances, a transfer shortcut, and recent history in one place.
[*] [B]Configurable daily boundary[/B] — the daily-visit day follows UTC (default), board time, or a fixed UTC offset; registration-day skip uses the same boundary.
[*] [B]History pruning[/B] — summarize old ledger rows into balance snapshots and delete them; balances and rebuilds stay exact. New retention option and AdminCP tool; redeem/backfill rows are kept.
[*] [B]Top credit holders widget[/B] — a placeable leaderboard by balance, with a configurable count and currency.
[*] [B]Tests[/B] — DST/boundary unit tests and a DB-backed prune integration suite.
[/LIST]


